---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {url,evidence,articleBySlug} from '../lib/content';
import timeline from '../data/timeline.json';
const frontier=[['USB service readiness','A sampled stock listener follows early host preflight. Ordinary pairing, info, syslog, AFC and two-boot behavior are pending.','native-iphone','E54'],['Camera and graphics performance','The legacy two-versus-six queue comparison is physical; 7E18 preview throughput and animation performance remain unmeasured.','measuring-performance','E50'],['Sensors and ordinary restart','Real raw accelerometer samples and one direct reset are narrower than stock rotation or repeated owner restart acceptance.','buttons','E55'],['Next systems and peripherals','6.1.6 leads the conditional feasibility ranking; its QEMU entry still panics at a clock gate. GPU, modem, audio and networking remain open.','native-iphone','E58']];
---
<Base title="Research timeline" description="Follow the dated research records from reference identification through physical interaction, Camera preview and saved photographs, with open questions and reading paths.">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="section-number">SEQUENCE / OBSERVATION / NEXT QUESTION</span><h1>How the evidence<br/>became a system.</h1><p>Follow the dated records, then inspect the contracts behind each step. Progress in one environment does not move every other environment to the same point.</p></header>
<div class="timeline-intro"><p><strong>Two clocks, kept separate.</strong> Dates below identify dated reports in the reviewed corpus. Elapsed seconds and frame sequence numbers belong only to their named experiment. Work overlapped; this is a reading chronology, not a claim that every subsystem advanced in a single linear run.</p><a class="text-link" href="#frontier">What remains open ↓</a></div>
<ol class="research-timeline">{timeline.map((event,i)=>{const record=evidence.find(e=>e.id===event.evidence)!;return <li id={'day-'+event.date+(timeline.findIndex(e=>e.date===event.date)===i?'':'-'+event.evidence)}><div class="timeline-date"><span class="mono">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><time datetime={event.date}>{event.date}</time><span>{record.environment}</span></div><div class="timeline-event"><h2>{event.title}</h2><p>{event.description}</p><div class="timeline-links"><a href={url(`evidence/${record.id}/`)}>Inspect {record.id} ↗</a><a href={url(`articles/${event.chapter}/`)}>Read: {articleBySlug(event.chapter)?.title} →</a></div></div></li>})}</ol>
<section class="timeline-sequence"><span class="section-number">WITHIN A SINGLE EXPERIMENT</span><h2>A display can advance, then deliberately go black.</h2><p>These are stages across explicitly identified captures, not timestamps from one continuous run. The mapped-capture sequence and the later blanking experiment answer different questions.</p><div class="capture-sequence"><a href={url('evidence/E16/#boot-capture')}><img src={url('evidence/images/E16-boot-seq1.png')} alt="QEMU scanout displaying the boot logo" width="320" height="480" loading="lazy"/><span class="mono">E16 / SEQUENCE 1</span><h3>Boot surface</h3><p>Selected surface A holds the boot logo.</p></a><a href={url('evidence/E16/#setup-capture')}><img src={url('evidence/images/E16-setup-seq5.png')} alt="QEMU scanout displaying the setup connection graphic" width="320" height="480" loading="lazy"/><span class="mono">E16 / SEQUENCE 5</span><h3>Client imagery</h3><p>After A → B → A, the selected surface contains setup pixels.</p></a><a href={url('evidence/E18/#blank-boundary')}><div class="blank-reference"><code>selected_surface = 0<br/>background = 0xff000000</code><span>Diagram from captured values</span></div><span class="mono">E18 / SEPARATE BLANKING RUN</span><h3>Intentional black</h3><p>Null presentation accompanies a dimming request; retained backing is checked separately.</p></a></div><p class="timeline-caption">The first two images are QEMU captures. The third panel is an original diagram of logged values, not a screenshot. <a href={url('evidence/E20/')}>The physical wake observation is E20.</a></p></section>
<section class="research-frontier" id="frontier"><span class="section-number">WHAT IS NEXT</span><h2>Questions the record still leaves open.</h2><p>These are documented research boundaries at the pinned snapshot. They are not claims that newer work has failed, or a live task queue for the ongoing experiment session.</p>{frontier.map(([title,description,slug,id])=><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p><a href={url(`articles/${slug}/`)}>Read the contract →</a><a href={url(`evidence/${id}/#limits`)}>Inspect the limit · {id} ↗</a></div>)}</section>
<nav class="timeline-reading" aria-label="Continue reading"><a class="button primary" href={url('tours/boot/')}>Read the continuous boot path →</a><a class="text-link" href={url('map/')}>Explore the connected graph ↗</a></nav>
</Base>
